Let's outline steps:

1. Release compliance certificate from shift_candidate_alpha to make it available.
2. Detach task profile from destination_availability_alpha to make route_task_profile_alpha available.
3. Attach task profile to origin_availability_alpha.
4. Confirm candidate preparedness for origin_availability_alpha (makes candidate_prepared true).
5. Assign operator resource to origin_availability_alpha (needs candidate_prepared).
6. Load origin payload (requires cargo_available, not origin_availability_locked). At this point origin_availability not locked yet (we haven't locked). Load will set origin_node_occupied true, origin_availability_locked true, origin_payload_linked, cargo unavailable.
7. Unload origin payload (requires origin_node_occupied, origin_payload_linked, not origin_availability_confirmed). After load, origin_availability_confirmed false, so unload precondition satisfied? Unload requires not origin_availability_confirmed ?origin_availability. After load, origin_availability_confirmed is false (since not set). So we can unload. Unload sets origin_node_ready true, origin_availability_confirmed true, cargo_available true, removes origin_payload_linked. Leaves origin_node_occupied true (unchanged) and origin_availability_locked true (unchanged). Good.
